---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import Nav from "../components/Nav.astro";
import Footer from "../components/Footer.astro";
---

<Base>
  <Fragment slot="head">
    <title>EasyHost: Free Node.js Hosting Your AI Agent Can Deploy To</title>
    <meta name="description" content="Free Node.js hosting for Next.js, Nuxt, Express, NestJS and more, with Postgres, S3 storage and custom domains. No credit card." />
    <link rel="canonical" href="https://easyhost.fun/" />
    <meta name="robots" content="index, follow, max-image-preview:large, max-snippet:-1" />
    <meta name="theme-color" content="#ffffff" />
    <meta property="og:type" content="website" />
    <meta property="og:site_name" content="EasyHost" />
    <meta property="og:url" content="https://easyhost.fun/" />
    <meta property="og:title" content="EasyHost: Free Node.js Hosting Your AI Agent Can Deploy To" />
    <meta property="og:description" content="Deploy Next.js, Nuxt, Express, NestJS and other Node.js frameworks with Postgres and S3 storage included." />
    <meta property="og:image" content="https://easyhost.fun/og.png" />
    <meta property="og:image:width" content="1200" />
    <meta property="og:image:height" content="630" />
    <meta property="og:image:alt" content="EasyHost: free Node.js hosting your AI agent can deploy to" />
    <meta name="twitter:card" content="summary_large_image" />
    <meta name="twitter:title" content="EasyHost: Free Node.js Hosting Your AI Agent Can Deploy To" />
    <meta name="twitter:description" content="Deploy Next.js, Nuxt, Express, NestJS and other Node.js frameworks with Postgres and S3 storage included." />
    <meta name="twitter:image" content="https://easyhost.fun/og.png" />
    <script is:inline type="application/ld+json">
      {
        "@context": "https://schema.org",
        "@graph": [
          {
            "@type": "Organization",
            "@id": "https://easyhost.fun/#organization",
            "name": "EasyHost",
            "url": "https://easyhost.fun/",
            "logo": "https://easyhost.fun/icon-512.png",
            "email": "hello@easyhost.fun",
            "sameAs": ["https://www.npmjs.com/package/ezhst"]
          },
          {
            "@type": "WebSite",
            "@id": "https://easyhost.fun/#website",
            "name": "EasyHost",
            "url": "https://easyhost.fun/",
            "publisher": { "@id": "https://easyhost.fun/#organization" }
          },
          {
            "@type": "SoftwareApplication",
            "@id": "https://easyhost.fun/#software",
            "name": "EasyHost",
            "url": "https://easyhost.fun/",
            "description": "Free hosting for Node.js apps with managed Postgres, S3 compatible storage and custom domains, operated through the ezhst CLI by AI coding agents.",
            "applicationCategory": "DeveloperApplication",
            "operatingSystem": "Web, macOS, Linux, Windows",
            "offers": { "@type": "Offer", "price": 0, "priceCurrency": "USD" },
            "publisher": { "@id": "https://easyhost.fun/#organization" }
          },
          {
            "@type": "FAQPage",
            "mainEntity": [
              {
                "@type": "Question",
                "name": "Is EasyHost really free?",
                "acceptedAnswer": { "@type": "Answer", "text": "Yes, for hosting. EasyHost hosting costs $0 per month and signing up does not need a credit card. It is included within fixed limits: 3 projects, and per project up to three apps, one Postgres database and one storage bucket. The AI Builder gives each account its first AI app and first build free, then uses AI Tokens you buy once (see pricing)." }
              },
              {
                "@type": "Question",
                "name": "What can I host on EasyHost?",
                "acceptedAnswer": { "@type": "Answer", "text": "Any framework that builds and runs as a Node.js service, including Next.js, Nuxt, Express, NestJS, Fastify, Hono, Koa, AdonisJS, Remix, SvelteKit, Astro and Strapi. SvelteKit and Astro need their Node adapters. HTTP apps must listen on 0.0.0.0 and the assigned PORT." }
              },
              {
                "@type": "Question",
                "name": "Do free apps go to sleep?",
                "acceptedAnswer": { "@type": "Answer", "text": "No. Each app runs in its own always-on container with 512 MB of RAM and 1 CPU. It is not stopped when idle, so there is no cold start on the first request." }
              },
              {
                "@type": "Question",
                "name": "Can I build an app without writing code?",
                "acceptedAnswer": { "@type": "Answer", "text": "Yes. Open the AI Builder in the dashboard, name your app and describe it. The AI asks a few questions, shows a plan, lets you pick a theme and builds a real Node.js app with Postgres and storage at its own address. Your first AI app and its first build are free; after that, AI requests use AI Tokens." }
              },
              {
                "@type": "Question",
                "name": "Which AI coding agents can deploy to EasyHost?",
                "acceptedAnswer": { "@type": "Answer", "text": "Any agent that can run shell commands. Run npx ezhst skill install, pick Claude Code, Codex or Cursor, then Global or Local. For any other agent, ask it to read the installed SKILL.md or https://easyhost.fun/skill.md before deploying." }
              },
              {
                "@type": "Question",
                "name": "Do I need to connect GitHub or change my project?",
                "acceptedAnswer": { "@type": "Answer", "text": "No. ezhst deploy packages the project folder and uploads it. There is no Git integration, no config file to write and no adapter to install." }
              },
              {
                "@type": "Question",
                "name": "Can I use my own domain?",
                "acceptedAnswer": { "@type": "Answer", "text": "Yes. Every project gets https://<name>.easyhost.fun, and you can add custom domains with ezhst domains add. HTTPS certificates are issued automatically once DNS is verified." }
              },
              {
                "@type": "Question",
                "name": "How is EasyHost different from Vercel?",
                "acceptedAnswer": { "@type": "Answer", "text": "Vercel runs Next.js on serverless functions behind a global CDN. EasyHost runs each app as one always-on container in a single region and includes Postgres and S3 storage in the same free account, all scriptable by a coding agent through one CLI. EasyHost has no preview deployments, Git integration or edge network." }
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      }
    </script>
  </Fragment>
    <Nav>
          <a href="#agents">For agents</a>
          <a href="#frameworks">Frameworks</a>
          <a href="#limits">Limits</a>
          <a href="#faq">FAQ</a>
          <a href="/docs" class="keep">Docs</a>
    </Nav>

    <main>
      <section class="hero">
        <div class="container hero-inner">
          <div>
            <p class="eyebrow reveal">Agent-first hosting. Free.</p>
            <h1 class="reveal reveal-1">Free Node.js hosting your AI agent can <mark>deploy&nbsp;to</mark>.</h1>
            <p class="lead reveal reveal-2">
              Tell your agent to ship it. It will. EasyHost is the first agent-first free hosting platform: Claude Code, Cursor, Codex and friends can create the account, deploy your Node.js app and wire up Postgres, S3 storage and domains through one CLI.
            </p>
            <div class="hero-actions reveal reveal-3">
              <a href="#agents" class="btn btn-primary btn-lg">Install the skill</a>
              <a href="/docs" class="btn btn-outline btn-lg">Read the docs</a>
            </div>
            <p class="hero-note reveal reveal-3">Prefer clicking? <a href="https://app.easyhost.fun/register">Sign up for the dashboard</a>.</p>
          </div>

          <div class="terminal reveal reveal-2">
            <div class="terminal-bar"><span></span><span></span><span></span><em>agent session</em></div>
            <pre><span class="you">you</span>  deploy this to EasyHost

<span class="muted">agent</span> <span class="cmd">$ ezhst whoami --json</span>
      Logged in as ada@example.com
      <span class="cmd">$ ezhst projects create my-app --json</span>
      <span class="cmd">$ ezhst link --project my-app</span>
      <span class="cmd">$ ezhst db create main --json</span>
      <span class="cmd">$ ezhst db info --json</span>
      <span class="cmd">$ ezhst env set DATABASE_URL=postgres://...</span>
      <span class="cmd">$ ezhst deploy --json</span>
      <span class="ok">done</span>  Uploaded, built, started

      Live at <b>https://my-app.easyhost.fun</b></pre>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section id="frameworks" class="section frameworks-section">
        <div class="container">
          <div class="frameworks-heading">
            <div>
              <p class="eyebrow">Bring your framework</p>
              <h2>If it runs on Node.js, it runs here.</h2>
            </div>
            <div>
              <p class="lead">EasyHost installs from your lockfile, runs the build script when you have one, and starts a production server on <code>$PORT</code>. No platform-specific runtime.</p>
              <div class="runtime-flow" aria-label="EasyHost deployment flow">
                <span>package.json</span><i>→</i><span>install</span><i>→</i><span>build</span><i>→</i><span>start</span>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="framework-grid" role="list" aria-label="Supported Node.js frameworks">
            <a class="framework-card" href="https://nextjs.org/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer" role="listitem">
              <span class="framework-logo"><img src="/frameworks/nextjs.svg" alt="" width="30" height="30" /></span>
              <span><strong>Next.js</strong><small>Auto-detected</small></span>
            </a>
            <a class="framework-card" href="https://nuxt.com/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer" role="listitem">
              <span class="framework-logo"><img src="/frameworks/nuxt.svg" alt="" width="30" height="30" /></span>
              <span><strong>Nuxt</strong><small>Auto-detected</small></span>
            </a>
            <a class="framework-card" href="https://expressjs.com/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer" role="listitem">
              <span class="framework-logo"><img src="/frameworks/express.svg" alt="" width="30" height="30" /></span>
              <span><strong>Express</strong><small>Start script</small></span>
            </a>
            <a class="framework-card" href="https://nestjs.com/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer" role="listitem">
              <span class="framework-logo"><img src="/frameworks/nestjs.svg" alt="" width="30" height="30" /></span>
              <span><strong>NestJS</strong><small>Start script</small></span>
            </a>
            <a class="framework-card" href="https://fastify.dev/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer" role="listitem">
              <span class="framework-logo"><img src="/frameworks/fastify.svg" alt="" width="30" height="30" /></span>
              <span><strong>Fastify</strong><small>Start script</small></span>
            </a>
            <a class="framework-card" href="https://hono.dev/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer" role="listitem">
              <span class="framework-logo"><img src="/frameworks/hono.svg" alt="" width="30" height="30" /></span>
              <span><strong>Hono</strong><small>Node server</small></span>
            </a>
            <a class="framework-card" href="https://koajs.com/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer" role="listitem">
              <span class="framework-logo"><img src="/frameworks/koa.svg" alt="" width="30" height="30" /></span>
              <span><strong>Koa</strong><small>Start script</small></span>
            </a>
            <a class="framework-card" href="https://adonisjs.com/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer" role="listitem">
              <span class="framework-logo"><img src="/frameworks/adonisjs.svg" alt="" width="30" height="30" /></span>
              <span><strong>AdonisJS</strong><small>Start script</small></span>
            </a>
            <a class="framework-card" href="https://remix.run/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer" role="listitem">
              <span class="framework-logo"><img src="/frameworks/remix.svg" alt="" width="30" height="30" /></span>
              <span><strong>Remix</strong><small>Start script</small></span>
            </a>
            <a class="framework-card" href="https://svelte.dev/docs/kit" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer" role="listitem">
              <span class="framework-logo"><img src="/frameworks/sveltekit.svg" alt="" width="30" height="30" /></span>
              <span><strong>SvelteKit</strong><small>Node adapter</small></span>
            </a>
            <a class="framework-card" href="https://astro.build/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer" role="listitem">
              <span class="framework-logo"><img src="/frameworks/astro.svg" alt="" width="30" height="30" /></span>
              <span><strong>Astro</strong><small>Node adapter</small></span>
            </a>
            <a class="framework-card" href="https://strapi.io/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer" role="listitem">
              <span class="framework-logo"><img src="/frameworks/strapi.svg" alt="" width="30" height="30" /></span>
              <span><strong>Strapi</strong><small>Start script</small></span>
            </a>
          </div>
          <p class="framework-note">Using something else? Add a production <code>start</code> script that listens on <code>0.0.0.0:$PORT</code>. Frameworks that generate provider-specific output need their Node adapter.</p>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section id="agents" class="section">
        <div class="container skill">
          <div>
            <p class="eyebrow">Step one</p>
            <h2>Give your agent the manual.</h2>
            <p class="lead">
              The EasyHost skill teaches your agent every <code>ezhst</code> command, when to use <code>--json</code>, and how to recover from a failed build. Install it once, then just ask.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div class="skill-steps">
            <div class="skill-step">
              <div class="skill-step-label">In your project</div>
              <div class="copy-line">
                <span><span class="prompt">$</span>npx ezhst skill install</span>
                <button class="copy" type="button" data-copy="npx ezhst skill install" aria-label="Copy command">
                  <svg class="icon icon-copy" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><rect width="14" height="14" x="8" y="8" rx="2" ry="2"/><path d="M4 16c-1.1 0-2-.9-2-2V4c0-1.1.9-2 2-2h10c1.1 0 2 .9 2 2"/></svg>
                  <svg class="icon icon-done" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M20 6 9 17l-5-5"/></svg>
                </button>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class="skill-step">
              <div class="skill-step-label">Then tell your agent</div>
              <div class="copy-line">
                <span><span class="prompt">&gt;</span>Deploy this to EasyHost</span>
                <button class="copy" type="button" data-copy="Deploy this to EasyHost" aria-label="Copy prompt">
                  <svg class="icon icon-copy" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><rect width="14" height="14" x="8" y="8" rx="2" ry="2"/><path d="M4 16c-1.1 0-2-.9-2-2V4c0-1.1.9-2 2-2h10c1.1 0 2 .9 2 2"/></svg>
                  <svg class="icon icon-done" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M20 6 9 17l-5-5"/></svg>
                </button>
              </div>
            </div>
            <p class="skill-foot">
              Pick Claude Code, Codex or Cursor, then Global for all projects or Local for this project. Add <code>--agent</code> and <code>--global</code> or <code>--local</code> to skip the prompts. If your agent does not discover the skill, ask it to read <a href="/skill.md">/skill.md</a>.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section id="capabilities" class="section section-muted">
        <div class="container">
          <div class="section-head">
            <div>
              <p class="eyebrow">What your agent can do</p>
              <h2>The whole platform, one authenticated CLI.</h2>
            </div>
            <p class="lead">Every command takes <code>--json</code> and never prompts without a terminal, so agents get clean output and clear errors.</p>
          </div>

          <div class="caps">
            <article class="cap">
              <span class="cap-icon"><svg class="icon" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M16 21v-2a4 4 0 0 0-4-4H6a4 4 0 0 0-4 4v2"/><circle cx="9" cy="7" r="4"/><line x1="19" x2="19" y1="8" y2="14"/><line x1="22" x2="16" y1="11" y2="11"/></svg></span>
              <div>
                <h3>Create an account</h3>
                <p>Register, verify with the 6-digit code from your inbox and log in, all without a browser.</p>
                <code>ezhst register --name --email --password</code>
              </div>
            </article>
            <article class="cap">
              <span class="cap-icon"><svg class="icon" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M4.5 16.5c-1.5 1.26-2 5-2 5s3.74-.5 5-2c.71-.84.7-2.13-.09-2.91a2.18 2.18 0 0 0-2.91-.09z"/><path d="m12 15-3-3a22 22 0 0 1 2-3.95A12.88 12.88 0 0 1 22 2c0 2.72-.78 7.5-6 11a22.35 22.35 0 0 1-4 2z"/><path d="M9 12H4s.55-3.03 2-4c1.62-1.08 5 0 5 0"/><path d="M12 15v5s3.03-.55 4-2c1.08-1.62 0-5 0-5"/></svg></span>
              <div>
                <h3>Deploy Node.js</h3>
                <p>Package the folder, upload, build and go live on its own subdomain.</p>
                <code>ezhst deploy</code>
              </div>
            </article>
            <article class="cap">
              <span class="cap-icon"><svg class="icon" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M8 3H7a2 2 0 0 0-2 2v5a2 2 0 0 1-2 2 2 2 0 0 1 2 2v5c0 1.1.9 2 2 2h1"/><path d="M16 21h1a2 2 0 0 0 2-2v-5c0-1.1.9-2 2-2a2 2 0 0 1-2-2V5a2 2 0 0 0-2-2h-1"/></svg></span>
              <div>
                <h3>Environment variables</h3>
                <p>Set, unset or import a whole .env file. Applied on the next deploy.</p>
                <code>ezhst env set KEY=VALUE</code>
              </div>
            </article>
            <article class="cap">
              <span class="cap-icon"><svg class="icon" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M20 7h-9"/><path d="M14 17H5"/><circle cx="17" cy="17" r="3"/><circle cx="7" cy="7" r="3"/></svg></span>
              <div>
                <h3>Build settings</h3>
                <p>Auto-detected by default. Override Node version, root dir or commands.</p>
                <code>ezhst build set --node 22</code>
              </div>
            </article>
            <article class="cap">
              <span class="cap-icon"><svg class="icon" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><polyline points="4 17 10 11 4 5"/><line x1="12" x2="20" y1="19" y2="19"/></svg></span>
              <div>
                <h3>Logs and build logs</h3>
                <p>Read runtime logs and the full build log, so the agent can fix what broke.</p>
                <code>ezhst deployments log</code>
              </div>
            </article>
            <article class="cap">
              <span class="cap-icon"><svg class="icon" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="10"/><path d="M12 2a14.5 14.5 0 0 0 0 20 14.5 14.5 0 0 0 0-20"/><path d="M2 12h20"/></svg></span>
              <div>
                <h3>Custom domains</h3>
                <p>Add a hostname, get the DNS record to set, verify and get HTTPS.</p>
                <code>ezhst domains add shop.example.com</code>
              </div>
            </article>
            <article class="cap">
              <span class="cap-icon"><svg class="icon" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><line x1="22" x2="2" y1="12" y2="12"/><path d="M5.45 5.11 2 12v6a2 2 0 0 0 2 2h16a2 2 0 0 0 2-2v-6l-3.45-6.89A2 2 0 0 0 16.76 4H7.24a2 2 0 0 0-1.79 1.11z"/><line x1="6" x2="6.01" y1="16" y2="16"/><line x1="10" x2="10.01" y1="16" y2="16"/></svg></span>
              <div>
                <h3>S3 storage</h3>
                <p>An S3 compatible bucket with public file URLs and its own keys.</p>
                <code>ezhst storage create uploads</code>
              </div>
            </article>
            <article class="cap">
              <span class="cap-icon"><svg class="icon" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><ellipse cx="12" cy="5" rx="9" ry="3"/><path d="M3 5V19A9 3 0 0 0 21 19V5"/><path d="M3 12A9 3 0 0 0 21 12"/></svg></span>
              <div>
                <h3>Postgres</h3>
                <p>A managed database with a connection string and a shadow DB for Prisma.</p>
                <code>ezhst db query "select 1"</code>
              </div>
            </article>
            <article class="cap">
              <span class="cap-icon"><svg class="icon" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M16 21v-2a4 4 0 0 0-4-4H6a4 4 0 0 0-4 4v2"/><circle cx="9" cy="7" r="4"/><path d="M22 21v-2a4 4 0 0 0-3-3.87"/><path d="M16 3.13a4 4 0 0 1 0 7.75"/></svg></span>
              <div>
                <h3>Team members</h3>
                <p>Invite people to a project by email. Members manage everything in it.</p>
                <code>ezhst members invite you@team.com</code>
              </div>
            </article>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section id="how" class="section">
        <div class="container">
          <p class="eyebrow">How it works</p>
          <h2>From a folder to a live URL in one sentence.</h2>
          <ol class="steps">
            <li>
              <span class="step-number">01</span>
              <h3>Install the skill</h3>
              <p>Run <code>npx ezhst skill install</code>, pick your agent, then Global or Local.</p>
            </li>
            <li>
              <span class="step-number">02</span>
              <h3>Ask your agent</h3>
              <p>"Deploy this to EasyHost." It signs you up if needed, creates a project and sets the env vars your app uses.</p>
            </li>
            <li>
              <span class="step-number">03</span>
              <h3>It goes live</h3>
              <p>We install, build and start your app. If a build fails, the agent reads the log, fixes it and redeploys.</p>
            </li>
          </ol>
          <div class="human">
            <p><strong>Humans get a dashboard too.</strong> Manage projects, deployments, storage and databases from the browser, or describe an app to the <a href="/products/ai-builder">AI Builder</a> and watch it build the frontend and backend live.</p>
            <a href="https://app.easyhost.fun/register" class="btn btn-outline">Open the dashboard</a>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section id="limits" class="section section-muted">
        <div class="container limits">
          <div>
            <p class="eyebrow">Limits</p>
            <h2>Free. These are the limits.</h2>
            <p class="lead">Hosting is free within these limits, with no credit card. The AI Builder includes your first AI app and build, then uses AI Tokens. EasyHost runs Node.js apps, including Next.js, Express, Fastify and other Node.js services.</p>
            <p class="price">$0 <span>/ month</span></p>
            <p class="limits-more">See what the <a href="/free-nextjs-hosting">free Next.js hosting</a> plan includes, or how it compares as a <a href="/vercel-alternative">Vercel alternative</a>.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="limit-table">
            <div class="limit-row"><span>Projects</span><b>3</b></div>
            <div class="limit-row"><span>Apps</span><b>3 per project</b></div>
            <div class="limit-row"><span>Storage buckets</span><b>1 per project</b></div>
            <div class="limit-row"><span>Postgres databases</span><b>1 per project</b></div>
            <div class="limit-row"><span>Team members</span><b>10 per project</b></div>
            <div class="limit-row"><span>AI Builder prompts</span><b>30 / day</b></div>
            <div class="limit-row"><span>AI Builder</span><b>First app and build free, then AI Tokens</b></div>
            <div class="limit-row"><span>Concurrent builds</span><b>1</b></div>
            <div class="limit-row"><span>App container</span><b>512 MB RAM, 1 CPU</b></div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section id="faq" class="section">
        <div class="container">
          <p class="eyebrow">FAQ</p>
          <h2>Questions people ask before they deploy.</h2>
          <div class="faq">
            <div>
              <h3>Is EasyHost really free?</h3>
              <p>Yes, for hosting. EasyHost hosting costs $0 per month and signing up does not need a credit card. It is included within fixed <a href="#limits">limits</a>: 3 projects, and per project up to three apps, one Postgres database and one storage bucket. The AI Builder gives each account its first AI app and first build free, then uses AI Tokens you buy once (see <a href="/pricing">pricing</a>).</p>
            </div>
            <div>
              <h3>What can I host on EasyHost?</h3>
              <p>Any framework that builds and runs as a Node.js service, including Next.js, Nuxt, Express, NestJS, Fastify, Hono, Koa, AdonisJS, Remix, SvelteKit, Astro and Strapi. SvelteKit and Astro need their Node adapters. HTTP apps must listen on <code>0.0.0.0</code> and the assigned <code>PORT</code>.</p>
            </div>
            <div>
              <h3>Do free apps go to sleep?</h3>
              <p>No. Each app runs in its own always-on container with 512 MB of RAM and 1 CPU. It is not stopped when idle, so there is no cold start on the first request.</p>
            </div>
            <div>
              <h3>Which AI coding agents can deploy to EasyHost?</h3>
              <p>Any agent that can run shell commands. Run <code>npx ezhst skill install</code> , pick Claude Code, Codex or Cursor, then Global or Local. For any other agent, ask it to read the installed <code>SKILL.md</code> or <a href="/skill.md">skill.md</a> before deploying. The <a href="/guides/deploy-nextjs-with-ai-agents">agent deploy guide</a> has the steps for each.</p>
            </div>
            <div>
              <h3>Do I need to connect GitHub or change my project?</h3>
              <p>No. <code>ezhst deploy</code> packages the project folder and uploads it. There is no Git integration, no config file to write and no adapter to install.</p>
            </div>
            <div>
              <h3>Can I use my own domain?</h3>
              <p>Yes. Every project gets <code>https://&lt;name&gt;.easyhost.fun</code>, and you can add <a href="/docs#domains">custom domains</a> with <code>ezhst domains add</code>. HTTPS certificates are issued automatically once DNS is verified.</p>
            </div>
            <div>
              <h3>How is EasyHost different from Vercel?</h3>
              <p>Vercel runs Next.js on serverless functions behind a global CDN. EasyHost runs each app as one always-on container in a single region and includes Postgres and S3 storage in the same free account, all scriptable by a coding agent through one CLI. EasyHost has no preview deployments, Git integration or edge network. Read the full <a href="/vercel-alternative">comparison</a>.</p>
            </div>
            <div>
              <h3>Can I build an app without writing code?</h3>
              <p>Yes. Open the <a href="/products/ai-builder">AI Builder</a> in the dashboard, name your app and describe it. The AI asks a few questions, shows a plan, lets you pick a theme and builds a real Node.js app with Postgres and storage at its own address. Your first AI app and its first build are free; after that, AI requests use AI Tokens.</p>
            </div>
            <div>
              <h3>Is the database a real Postgres?</h3>
              <p>Yes. Each project can have one Postgres 16 database with its own role, reachable over TLS with a standard connection string, plus a shadow database for <code>prisma migrate dev</code>. More on the <a href="/free-postgres-hosting">free Postgres hosting</a> page.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

